<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3927" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλεγύνω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		 Verb, <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only pres. and impf.: aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέγῡνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.394
				</span></i>
			, 
				Med.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλεγύνατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					137.4
				</span></i>
			 : (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέγω</span>) :—<i>heed,
				care for</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (only <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>) always c. acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαῖτα</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαῖτας, ἄλλας δ᾽ ἀλεγύνετε δαῖτας</span>
			<i>find</i> your meals elsewhere, <i><span class="en">
				1.374
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαῖτ᾽ ἀλέγυνον</span>, of
			invited guests, <i><span class="en">
				13.23
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαῖτας ἐΐσας . . ἀλεγύνειν</span>
			<i>prepare</i> a meal <i>for guests</i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.186
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δολοφροσύνην ἀλεγύνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					361
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγλαΐας ἀλέγυνε</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				476
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
